              "text": "bharati is the present of the root √bhṛ, \"to bear, carry, support\" (MW). The root is inherited from Indo-European: MW sets it beside Latin ferō and English bear. Through Prakrit it became Hindi bharnā, \"to fill\" (CDIAL 9397)."
