              "text": "vahati is the present of the root √vah, \"to carry, convey\", which also says what a river does with what it carries. The root is inherited from Indo-European: MW compares Latin vehere, the source of English vehicle. It lives on as Hindi bahnā, \"to flow\" (CDIAL 11453)."
